## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Test Method | Smell | Effort |
|----------|-------------|-------|--------|
| 1 | `addAndDoNothing` | Assertion-Free | Trivial — add one assertion |
| 2 | `addNullSkuManualCatch` | Exception Handling | Low — swap to `assertThrows` |
| 3 | `addSleepy` | Sleepy Test | Trivial — delete one line |
| 4 | `addLoadsFromFile` | Mystery Guest | Low — inline the string |
| 5 | `addConditionalLogic` | Conditional Logic | Low — flatten to explicit calls |
| 6 | `doEverythingAtOnce` | Eager Test | Medium — split into focused tests |
| 7 | `quantityAfterAdds` | Magic Number | Low — use named constants |
| 8 | `toStringFormat` | Sensitive Equality | Low — assert structure, not format |
| 9 | `setUp` / `rng` | General Fixture | Trivial — delete unused field |
| 10 | `disabledTest` | Ignored Test | Decision — fix or delete |

Items 1–5 are quick wins (< 5 minutes each) that eliminate all **High**-severity smells and most flakiness risk.
